<%# Visual coverage for the responsive variant axis.
    The other visual fixtures pin one device and one orientation, and every one
    of them hardcodes screen--landscape, a class the picker never emits. That
    combination is exactly what let a broken landscape gate ship unnoticed.
    These cases vary size and orientation instead, and deliberately carry no
    explicit orientation class in the landscape rows so the framework default
    is what gets photographed. %>
<%# sm is the tightest size class the framework has, so it is where clamping,
    overflow and gap collapse are most likely to look wrong. Its device is
    amazon_kindle_2024, the one profile core exports at that size, and it brings
    a 0.8 device ui-scale with it.

    New cases go on the end. Playwright scrolls each case into view before it
    clips the screenshot, so inserting a row above one moves it down the document
    and re-rasterizes its text against a different subpixel offset. Four baselines
    went red the first time these two rows led the list. %>
<% responsive_modes = [
  ['responsive-md-landscape', 'screen--og', 800, 480],
  ['responsive-md-portrait', 'screen--og screen--portrait', 480, 800],
  ['responsive-lg-landscape', 'screen--v2 screen--lg', 1040, 780],
  ['responsive-lg-portrait', 'screen--v2 screen--lg screen--portrait', 780, 1040],
  ['responsive-sm-landscape', 'screen--amazon_kindle_2024 screen--sm', 800, 480],
  ['responsive-sm-portrait', 'screen--amazon_kindle_2024 screen--sm screen--portrait', 480, 800]
] %>

<style>
  .visual-responsive-screen {
    position: relative !important;
    min-height: 0 !important;
    margin: 0 !important;
    transform: none !important;
  }
</style>

<main class="visual-page" data-visual-ready="true">
  <% responsive_modes.each do |visual_id, screen_classes, width, height| %>
    <div id="<%= visual_id %>" class="trmnl" data-visual
         style="width: <%= width %>px; height: <%= height %>px;">
      <div class="screen screen--1bit <%= screen_classes %> visual-responsive-screen"
           style="width: <%= width %>px !important; height: <%= height %>px !important;">
        <div class="view view--full">
          <%# Direction, gap, and column count all swing on orientation, so a
              dead orientation gate rearranges the whole frame. %>
          <div class="layout layout--row portrait:layout--col gap--small lg:gap--large">
            <div class="grid grid--cols-2 portrait:grid--cols-1 lg:grid--cols-3 gap--small">
              <div class="item rounded bg--gray-70 landscape:bg--gray-40 p--3">
                <div class="content">
                  <span class="value value--large lg:value--xlarge value--tnums">42</span>
                  <span class="label label--small portrait:label--outline">Landscape ink</span>
                </div>
              </div>
              <div class="item rounded bg--gray-55 p--3">
                <div class="content">
                  <span class="value value--large portrait:value--xxlarge value--tnums">7</span>
                  <span class="label label--small">Portrait ink</span>
                </div>
              </div>
              <div class="item rounded bg--gray-35 p--3 md:flex--center">
                <div class="content">
                  <span class="value value--large value--tnums">13</span>
                  <span class="label label--small">Alignment</span>
                </div>
              </div>
            </div>

            <%# Table sizes took orientation variants late; this pins the rows. %>
            <table class="table table--xsmall lg:table--base lg:portrait:table--xlarge">
              <thead>
                <tr><th><span class="title title--small">Job</span></th><th><span class="title title--small">State</span></th></tr>
              </thead>
              <tbody>
                <tr><td><span class="label">build</span></td><td><span class="label label--filled">ok</span></td></tr>
                <tr><td><span class="label">deploy</span></td><td><span class="label label--inverted">queued</span></td></tr>
              </tbody>
            </table>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  <% end %>
</main>
